--
User-reported: GNU array designators `[idx] = val` in C++ (accepted
by g++ and clang++), here in `static constexpr uint8_t sz[3] = {[0]
= 1, [1] = 8, [2] = 1}`.  The parser only knew C++20 `.member`
designators; the array form is built in the C front end's
ID_index/ID_designator shape.  Also fixed alongside: a constexpr
static ARRAY member is a definition (N5008 [class.static.data]/3),
not an extern macro -- it was never statically initialised and every
`A::sz[i]` read nondet (also without designators).
